result.description:
Outback Honey  is an Australian owned and operated apiary located in Dubbo New South Wales. It produces Australian certified organic honey. 

 The business is now offering a full time position to candidates with the necessary skilled experience. The candidates must provide evidence of at least three years’ skilled experience working as an apiarist/beekeeper. 

 The duties of the position include: 


	 Breeding and raising queen bees; 
	 Monitoring and maintaining the health and condition of the bees; 
	 Checking and re-queening bee hives regularly; 
	 Providing and maintaining appropriate nutritional environment; 
	 Producing, harvesting and extracting honey/honeycomb; 
	 Royal Jelly, Pollen, Bees was and propolis production; 
	 Planning and organising for brood nest management operation; 
	 Inspecting bee sites for good breeding condition and honey production; 
	 Coordinating farmers for pollination services; 
	 Destroying superfluous queen bee cells to prevent division of colony by swarming. 


 The successful applicant is expected to have skilled experience in the above-listed duties,  be of good character, free from allergies, and willing to comply with industry WHS and quality assurance standards and expectations. 

 Please provide a resume and a covering letter explaining why you will be an ideal candidate for the position. 

 Only those short-listed will be contacted. 

 Job Types: Full-time, Permanent 

 Salary Range - $80,000 - $90,000 p.a.

Applications close on 12/08/26
